2:21:10Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I get this error trying to use pprint via vcpkg:\r\n```\r\nError in projectName/CMakeLists.txt:\r\n  Imported target \"pprint::pprint\" includes non-existent path\r\n\r\n    \"/include\"\r\n\r\n  in its INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES.  Possible reasons include:\r\n\r\n  * The path was deleted, renamed, or moved to another location.\r\n\r\n  * An install or uninstall procedure did not complete successfully.\r\n\r\n  * The installation package was faulty and references files it does not\r\n  provide.\r\n```\r\n\r\nI changed line 57 in vcpkg\\installed\\x64-windows\\share\\pprint\\pprintConfig.cmake :\r\n```cmake\r\nset_target_properties(pprint::pprint PROPERTIES\r\n  INTERFACE_COMPILE_FEATURES \"cxx_std_17\"\r\n  INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES \"${_IMPORT_PREFIX}/include;/include\"\r\n)\r\n```\r\nto\r\n```cmake\r\nset_target_properties(pprint::pprint PROPERTIES\r\n  INTERFACE_COMPILE_FEATURES \"cxx_std_17\"\r\n  INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES \"${_IMPORT_PREFIX}/include;\"\r\n)\r\n```\r\nand that fixed my problem. I am not sure which file to modify in the vcpkg or pprint repo so that this file changes correctly, or even if this is safe to do without creating new problems.","closed_by":{"login":"dan-shaw","id":51385773,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzg1Nzcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51385773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-shaw","html_url":"https://github.com/dan-shaw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-shaw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-shaw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-shaw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-shaw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":